        <body>
            <div xml:id="d56">

                <pb facs="0076" n="70" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg70"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Uhl to Mr.
                            Goschen.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 57.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-10-10"><hi rendition="#italic">October 10,
                        1894</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 6th instant, asking whether the Government of the United
                    States would be willing to join with England, Germany, France, and Russia in
                    intervening between China and Japan.</p>
                <p>In reply I beg to inform you that the subject will be brought to the attention of
                    the President.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwin F. Uhl.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
